From: Soe Thura <6492082+thixpin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:23:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Decode VMX128 before PowerPC 405 instructions for Cell

The decoder's default dialect, which the cell option leaves in place, includes the PowerPC
403/405 instructions. Their encodings overlap VMX128: in Forza Motorsport 4, one vsldoi128 word
decodes as the 405 multiply-accumulate mullhwu. and is not translated. Cell and Xenon have no
403/405 instructions, so the cell dialect no longer enables them. Across all of FM4's code
words, that word is the only decode that changes.
---
 thirdparty/disasm/ppc-dis.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/thirdparty/disasm/ppc-dis.c b/thirdparty/disasm/ppc-dis.c
index 3e224b4..0ec6204 100644
--- a/thirdparty/disasm/ppc-dis.c
+++ b/thirdparty/disasm/ppc-dis.c
@@ -5336,6 +5336,12 @@ powerpc_dialect(struct disassemble_info* info)
         && strstr(info->disassembler_options, "440") != NULL)
         dialect |= PPC_OPCODE_BOOKE | PPC_OPCODE_32
         | PPC_OPCODE_440 | PPC_OPCODE_ISEL | PPC_OPCODE_RFMCI;
+    else if (info->disassembler_options
+        && strstr(info->disassembler_options, "cell") != NULL)
+        /* Cell and Xenon lack the PowerPC 403/405 instructions, whose encodings (e.g. 405
+           mullhwu.) would otherwise shadow VMX128 ones (vsldoi128).  */
+        dialect |= (PPC_OPCODE_601 | PPC_OPCODE_CLASSIC
+            | PPC_OPCODE_COMMON | PPC_OPCODE_ALTIVEC);
     else
         dialect |= (PPC_OPCODE_403 | PPC_OPCODE_601 | PPC_OPCODE_CLASSIC
             | PPC_OPCODE_COMMON | PPC_OPCODE_ALTIVEC);
